# Install Node Exporter

Node Exporter is installed on the **Target Server**.

Node Exporter exposes operating-system and hardware metrics that Prometheus can collect.

Official download page:

https://prometheus.io/download/

### Download Node Exporter

```bash
sudo -i

wget https://github.com/prometheus/node_exporter/releases/download/v1.4.0-rc.0/node_exporter-1.4.0-rc.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
```

Extract:

```bash
tar -zxvf node_exporter-1.4.0-rc.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
```

Installation directory:

```text
/root/node_exporter-1.4.0-rc.0.linux-amd64
```

---

# Create Node Exporter Systemd Service

Create:

```bash
sudo vi /etc/systemd/system/node_exporter.service
```

Add:

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Node Exporter
Documentation=https://prometheus.io/docs/guides/node-exporter/
After=network-online.target

[Service]
User=root
Restart=on-failure

ExecStart=/root/node_exporter-1.4.0-rc.0.linux-amd64/node_exporter

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

Reload systemd:

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
```

Start Node Exporter:

```bash
sudo systemctl start node_exporter
```

Check status:

```bash
sudo systemctl status node_exporter
```

Enable at boot:

```bash
sudo systemctl enable node_exporter
```

Check the target server's hostname and IP:

```bash
hostname
hostname -i
```

Node Exporter listens on:

```text
9100
```

