# Install Grafana

Grafana is installed on the **Monitoring Server**.

Official website:

https://grafana.com/

For a Red Hat/CentOS/RHEL/Fedora-based system, install the RPM package:

```bash
sudo yum install -y https://dl.grafana.com/oss/release/grafana-11.1.0-1.x86_64.rpm
```

Enable Grafana:

```bash
sudo systemctl enable grafana-server.service
```

Start Grafana:

```bash
sudo systemctl start grafana-server.service
```

Check status:

```bash
sudo systemctl status grafana-server.service
```

Grafana Web UI:

```text
http://<GRAFANA_PUBLIC_IP>:3000
```

---

# Configure Prometheus as Grafana Data Source

Login to Grafana:

```text
http://<GRAFANA_PUBLIC_IP>:3000
```

Go to:

```text
Settings
    ↓
Data Sources
    ↓
Add Data Source
    ↓
Prometheus
```

Enter a name:

```text
Prometheus
```

Enter the Prometheus URL.

If Grafana and Prometheus are installed on the **same server**, preferably use:

```text
http://localhost:9090
```

If they are on separate servers:

```text
http://<PROMETHEUS_PRIVATE_IP>:9090
```

Click:

```text
Save & Test
```

A successful connection confirms that Grafana can communicate with Prometheus.

